This project is an independent implementation. It shares a goal with Locus
(https://github.com/farlocus/locus, GPL-3.0-or-later) — exposing Unity, Blender
and LaTeX to a coding agent — but contains no Locus source code. The wire
protocol, the Unity package and the Blender add-on were written from scratch
and are released under MIT.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components

1. Roslyn (Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.Scripting 3.8.0)
   Files: unity-package/Editor/Roslyn/*.dll (staged locally, not committed)
   Copyright (c) .NET Foundation and Contributors
   Licensed under the MIT License.
   https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn
   Not modified. Redistributed unmodified when you run
   scripts/sync-roslyn.mjs; that directory is git-ignored, so a source
   release carries no binaries.

2. DeepSeek Harness plugin conventions
   No @deepseek-ai/* packages are imported at runtime; the bundle only relies
   on the Cordis plugin context that the host passes to apply(ctx, config).

